{
  "id": "06111_kakeoriru",
  "headword": "{駆|か}け{下|お}りる",
  "reading": "かけおりる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan, intransitive)",
  "gloss": "to run down; to dash down",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{駆|か}け{下|お}り"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to run down; to dash down",
      "explanation": "To run quickly downward, such as descending stairs, a hill, or a slope at speed."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06111_kakeoriru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{階段|かいだん}を{駆|か}け{下|お}りる。",
      "english": "To run down the stairs.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06111_kakeoriru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{山道|やまみち}を{駆|か}け{下|お}りてきた。",
      "english": "He came running down the mountain path.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06111_kakeoriru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{危|あぶ}ないから{駆|か}け{下|お}りないで。",
      "english": "It's dangerous, so don't run down.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB:\n{駆|か}ける (to run, to gallop) + {下|お}りる (to go down, to descend)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive) - takes を for the path being traversed\n\nALTERNATE FORMS:\nAlso written as {駆|か}け{降|お}りる using a different kanji for おりる.\n\nRELATED COMPOUND VERBS:\n- {駆|か}け{上|あ}がる: to run up\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}む: to rush in\n- {駆|か}け{回|まわ}る: to run around\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {階段|かいだん}を{駆|か}け{下|お}りる: to run down the stairs\n- {坂|さか}を{駆|か}け{下|お}りる: to run down a slope",
